00:00:02.629 --> 00:00:05.110 align:start position:0%
horizon forbidden west offers way more  combat options than in horizon zero dawn  and that can be daunting with a bunch of  new weapons items and abilities on offer  let me help you take out anything or  anyone that stands in your way with some  useful combat tips if you enjoy horizon  forbidden west content let us know with  a like  valor surges are one of the most useful  new techniques in horizon forbidden west  and can be multifunctional valor surges  not only have amazing effects when  activated you're invincible during the  cool animation itself so it's great as a  defensive measure  any valor surge when timed will can be  used to dodge deadly attacks and on top  of that you can use this time to d-pad  up and start healing yourself with  berries during the animation giving you  a head start on your self-patching  progress in horizon zero dawn dodge  rolling was the main state of dodging  attacks giving you invincibility frames  but sliding was somewhat of an  afterthought not giving too much value  in combat forbidden west has upped the  ante by making sliding an essential  skill and making it invincible for a  short time as well so to maximize on  your dodge time first hit the ground  running  then slide then dodge roll this entire  duration is completely immune to attacks  and basically doubles your distance  traveled and time spent invincible  if you're a big fan of tripwires and  zero dawn i've got some bad news for you  they've been nerfed pretty bad the  damage is still great but the placement  has been heavily toned down with  tripwires breaking much more often if  you space them too far apart placed at  odd angles or on strange terrain also  all traps in general compared to zero  dawn can be self-triggered this time  around so keep this in mind as you're  trying to surprise the enemy if you're  not careful you might eat a face full of  your own plants  there are skills to unlock to reduce the  damage done to yourself so if you're  adamant about maximizing your trapping  pick these perks first because blowing  yourself up is bound to happen  there are a ton of ways to customize  your experience in the settings in  forbidden west so here are some key ones  for combat that you may want to consider  turning on or off while playing the game  try messing around with the weapon wheel  slow down speeds initially the normal  speed doesn't slow down the game much  but turning it down to the slowest  setting will give you much more time to  think about your equipment switch while  in a hectic fight another setting i  personally recommend is the weapon quick  swap option especially if you like  swapping between two weapons over and  over this will ease the headache of  going into the menu every single time it  allows you to switch between your last  two weapons by just tapping l1 instead  of holding it down and pulling up the  weapon wheel if you're playing on ps5  mess around with some test fights with  favorite performance or favor resolution  although horizon isn't a one frame link  intensive fighting game by all means the  extra frames do help alloy feel a little  more snappy during battles so test out  your preference and see what fits you  best  one of forbidden west's new weapons the  javelin is probably more useful than you  think their hefty payload not only does  damage on impact but very often stuns  enemies for a brief second against very  aggressive enemies this stun comes very  clutch and if you get explosive javelins  they get stun and damage on impact and  stun and damage on explosion and  absolutely destroy armor i highly  recommend always having some javelins in  your equipment wheel  jump off attacks are a new addition to  aeloy's melee combat repertoire by  holding heavy attack right after a  single light attack this will plant your  feet on the enemy and jump off of them  striking them with an arrow during this  jump off will do extra damage as well  leading to a fancy combo always remember  that the jump off direction is  influenced by which direction you hold  after planting your feet so for the best  arrow follow-up option hold back towards  you otherwise you'll jump forward  forcing you to do a full 360 to do this  follow-up option which is a royal pain  one advanced technique i ran into is the  half moon cancel holding a light attack  will charge up aloy's spear this can be  released into an attack that rushes down  enemies and slashes for decent damage  called the half moon slash a side note  this can be used to link into the  aforementioned jump off attack  cool thing though is the moment the half  moon slash is released you can jump or  roll so who cares well this leads to  some really cool options such as double  jump attacks or double rolling pretty  nifty so combine your slide and hold  light attack then dodge roll then  release attack and dodge roll a second  time for a really long evasive window  when it comes to valor surges you may  pick and choose many options based on  how you play which is really nice  whether it be you prefer stealth high  defense options or for me i like high  offense and damage capabilities you can  preview these perk upgrades by pressing  triangle over each valor surge during  your choosing process though remember  that each valor surge has three levels  and on the final third level when  unlocked usually has an extra ability  that really might change your mind for  better or for worse level three critical  boost gives a little more critical  damage and chance or level three tough  end to negates blind and defin status  not bad i guess but compare those two to  something like melee might which gives  infinite spear energy and a bunch of  knock down capabilities basically the  ability to completely cover enemies and  resonator blasts for satisfying bubble  wrap popping follow-ups  or radial blast which not only does  insane damage by itself and looks  amazing but also doubles all your damage  on follow-up attacks for 15 seconds or  chain burst which on paper doesn't sound  quite as fun as some massive electrical  explosion until you find out that it has  the best crowd control ability that's  borderline broken  not only does damage and elemental build  up spread out towards multiple enemies  but the small stun it does also spreads  to every enemy as well  basically locking down an entire squad  all this gameplay is on very hard mode  by the way showing just how powerful  this is just make sure to do your  homework first and read every  description so you know what to  prioritize first if not at least make a  save with skill points stocked up so you  can give each fowler upgrade a trial run  in real combat and if one's not your cup  of tea simply reload your save and build  something you prefer  smoke bombs are an obvious way to escape  enemies with a distraction for a brief  moment even usable underwater like a  squid using ink to escape but they can  also be used offensively against some  enemies to give you a window to sneak  strike them  just keep in mind this won't work  against tougher enemies  when using grapple points get in the  consistent rhythm of grappling then  pressing dodge to jump off vertically in  combat this is a nice vantage point to  keep you on the move and get a shot off  on enemies from above with a caveat if  you land you'll get stuck in a super  long landing animation making you easy  pickings for any enemy wanting to come  by and give ailoy a knock on the head  so get in the habit of gliding then  going for a shot or vice versa shooting  then gliding back down to keep the flow  of combat going or you can tap or hold  l2 to be in aiming mode while landing to  negate landing lag entirely although i  believe this is a bug so it may be  patched at some point  and there you have it 10 combat tips to  help you dominate the forbidden west let  us know if any of these tips helped and  if you enjoy horizon forbidden west we  have a full story recap and graphics  comparison for you to check out for  everything else gaming keep it here on  gamespot
 

